patch: interp/stdin_os.go — newPipe and newStdinFile call pipeFunc, which
       defaults to os.Pipe; interp.SetPipeFunc replaces it. On GOOS=wasip1
       os.Pipe is ENOSYS, so the interpreter could not run a pipeline, a
       here-document or a non-file stdin; the shell passes wasix.Pipe
       (WASIX fd_pipe).
to drop it: upstream an equivalent hook (or wasip1 pipes in Go), then
       remove the replace directive in ../../go.mod and this directory.
